{
	"_about": "Colour is a budget the days spend. One entry per day and phase drives every shader and the ambient light. Hex colours; saturation 0..1 scales the sky, sea and accents; ambient multiplies the whole frame (CanvasModulate); sun_x places the sun or moon across the screen (0..1 from the left) and sun_y down the sky as a fraction of the height above the horizon (0 the top, 1 on the horizon, more than 1 set); sun_size and sun_glow shape it; stars 0..1; haze_alpha is the band over the horizon; tint, grain and vignette feed the print pass; ground colours every Polygon2D in the \"ground\" group (sand, road), bright by day and near-black at night.",
